10	 candidates without widening the element's security boundary.
11	 <p>
12	 The attribute value is a comma-separated list of size entries. Entries are split on top-level commas only: a comma
13	 nested inside a balanced pair of parentheses (a media condition, or a {@code calc()} length) belongs to the entry
14	 that opened the parentheses. Each entry has an optional media condition followed by a required length value:
15	 </p>
16	 <ul>
17	 <li>an optional media condition is a non-empty, parenthesis-balanced parenthesized expression containing only
18	     letters, digits, whitespace, hyphens, colons, dots, comparison characters ({@code < = > ! /}), and nested
19	     parentheses. A semicolon, brace, quote, control character, or any other character invalidates the entry;</li>
20	 <li>the length is either a zero or a non-negative decimal number immediately followed by one of
21	     {@code px, em, rem, vw, vh, vmin, vmax, ch, ex, %} (e.g. {@code 100vw}, {@code 0px}, {@code 1.5em}), or a
22	     balanced {@code calc()} expression whose body contains only digits, dots, whitespace, the {@code + - * /}
23	     operators, nested parentheses, and the listed units. A URL, a semicolon, a brace, a leading minus, an empty
24	     length, or an unbalanced parenthesis invalidates the entry.</li>
