28	 references have already been decoded by the parser); the delimiting quotes are syntax only and never appear in the
29	 cleaned output. One malformed entry is dropped on its own and never swallows a following valid entry: after an
30	 unbalanced parenthesis, parsing resynchronizes at the next comma. Accepted entries are trimmed and joined in input
31	 order with a stable {@code ", "} separator; duplicate media conditions are kept as separate entries. When no entry
32	 survives, the attribute must be removed rather than left empty.
